diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b93024e..748b71c 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -109,7 +109,47 @@ Two things are worth knowing:
 * **`.rep` `int` becomes Nim `int32`, never `int`.** Nim's `int` is 64-bit and would reach the meta object as `qlonglong`, silently mismatching every replica generated from the same `.rep`.
 * **`READONLY` constrains the replica, not the source.** The generated source still gets a setter, since it is what publishes changes; only `CONSTANT` produces neither setter nor notify signal.
 
-`class`, `PROP`, `SLOT` and `SIGNAL` are supported. `POD`, `MODEL`, `ENUM`, nested `CLASS` and `USE_ENUM` are rejected by name rather than quietly dropped — `ENUM` in particular because `nimside` does not yet emit enums into the meta object. Replica-side generation is not implemented.
+`ENUM` is supported too, and generates a Nim enum alongside the type:
+
+```
+class Worker
+{
+    ENUM Status { Idle, Busy = 2, Failed = 7 }
+
+    PROP(Status status READONLY)
+}
+```
+
+becomes
+
+```nim
+qobject:
+  type
+    Status* {.pure, size: 4.} = enum
+      Idle = 0
+      Busy = 2
+      Failed = 7
+
+    Worker* {.qclassinfo(…), qenums(Status).} =
+      ref object of VirtualQObject
+        status {.qproperty(write = true, notify = true).}: Status
+```
+
+Keys carry the values the interface declares rather than their position, and `size: 4` matches Qt's int-sized enumerators — Nim would otherwise pick the smallest type the values fit in, and a one-byte enum read out of a four-byte slot is wrong everywhere except by accident on a little-endian machine.
+
+`class`, `PROP`, `SLOT`, `SIGNAL` and `ENUM` are supported. `POD`, `MODEL`, nested `CLASS` and `USE_ENUM` are rejected by name rather than quietly dropped. Replica-side generation is not implemented.
+
+### Signatures
+
+Pass `--signature` to have the generated type carry `QCLASSINFO_REMOTEOBJECT_SIGNATURE`:
+
+```sh
+rep2nim worker.rep --signature:696246f47f3498dd59631d8f51f78ae03f54755c
+```
+
+Take the value from the replica `repc` generates for the same `.rep`, where it appears as a literal — recomputing the hash would mean tracking repc's algorithm across Qt versions.
+
+It matters more than it looks: `QRemoteObjectNodePrivate::checkSignatures` treats an *empty* signature as "dynamic, do not verify", so without one an interface mismatch between the Nim source and its replica surfaces as silently wrong data rather than `SignatureMismatch`.
 
