+func metaTypeName*(T: type): string =
+  ## The Qt type name to record for `T`.
+  ##
+  ## Enums are recorded as `int`, which is what they are on the wire and in
+  ## storage. Recording the enum's own name instead would leave the meta type
+  ## unresolved -- Qt has no registered type for a Nim enum -- and an unresolved
+  ## meta type cannot be read or written through the meta object at all, so the
+  ## value would simply never propagate.
+  ##
